{"id":"u-d6f2bd67-f06a-4e56-90f2-36c0bdf4ef04","src":"community","title":"The Dorito Program","author":"Phillip M.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/VVeEqY-the-dorito-program","desc":"The Dorito Program is built for one goal: creating the classic powerful V-taper physique — broad shoulders, thick upper back, dense chest, strong arms, and a tight-looking waist. This is not a balanced athletic program, a marathon runner’s routine, or a minimalist fitness trend. It’s unapologetically upper-body dominant training designed for lifters who want to look imposing in and out of a shirt.\n\nThe foundation of the program revolves around heavy compound lifts, aggressive progressive overload, and high-volume shoulder and back work to maximize width and upper body density. Pressing movements build a thick chest and powerful delts, while rows, pull-ups, and lat-focused work develop the wide-frame look that gives the program its name.\n\nLeg training is intentionally streamlined — enough work to build strength, stability, and maintain proportional development without stealing recovery resources from upper body growth. The goal is functional lower body strength that supports the bigger mission: building the silhouette of a blacksmith, warrior, or comic-book brute.\n\nThe Dorito Program blends strength and hypertrophy principles to create a physique that is both powerful and visually intimidating. Heavy lifts develop raw force production while targeted accessory work hammers the shoulders, lats, traps, and arms for maximum visual impact.\n\nThis program rewards consistency, intensity, and effort. Show up, lift heavy, recover hard, and earn the shape.","level":["Beginner","Intermediate","Novice"],"goals":["Muscle","Strength"],"equipment":["Garage Gym"],"minutes":60,"joins":0,"rate":0,"rateCount":1,"updated":"2026-05-21T03:29:24.111Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Chest focus","Back with arm finisher","Shoulder focus","Back accessories then arms"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n"